# Build context exclusions.
#
# This file is a sibling of .gitignore, not a copy of it. .gitignore keeps things out of
# the repository; this keeps them out of the image. The two lists overlap because the
# same artifacts are unwanted in both, and the consequence here is worse: a build context
# is sent to the daemon and anything in it can be baked into a published layer.
#
# A local certification run writes its output under the package directory. Before this
# file covered it, a developer's own run output entered the context and the image: 2.0 GB
# of report data carrying provider endpoints, identifiers and payloads. Continuous
# integration never saw it, because it builds from a clean checkout, so the only machine
# that could notice was one with real run data on it. Provider data is excluded here by
# default, and a new output path is added to this list at the same time it is added to
# .gitignore.

# Dependencies and build output — rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage

# Version control and editor state
**/.git
**/.gitignore
.vscode
**/.DS_Store

# Certification run output — carries provider endpoints, identifiers and payloads
**/out
**/.reso-cert
**/reso-replication-output
**/vendor-logs
**/data-availability*.json
**/metadata-report*.json
**/data-dictionary*.json
**/schema-validation-report.json
**/upi-validation-report.json
**/reso-variations.json
**/compliance-results.zip
**/*.resoscript

# Run logs — every query URL, so every provider endpoint
**/*.log

# Credentials and local configuration
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
**/.mcp.json

# Local databases
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# Local tooling state
**/.packs
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
reso-certification/.venv-dd-lint

# Working notes that are not part of any image
PLAN.md
PR.md
**/results.*
lefthook-local.yml

# Sample fixtures are intentional and tracked, so the patterns above must not take them
!sample-reports
